PATCH 464: the 22dd display-list OBJECT-RENDER pass 286e + the per-node reticle hit-test 403f (board:0012
windshield-object frontier, slice 1).

With patches 462/463 the render walk now links real object nodes, so 286e runs for the first time: Ghidra
deref'd the node-list head word[0x4b9e] as a host int* (SEGV fault-addr 0x4bd64bde = two node offsets) and
read the record kind byte through it.  asm 0x286e-0x28b6: viewport bind (lcall [0x664]), then per node
`al=byte[bx+4]; call word[0x4b2c+al]` (the per-KIND rasterizer table), `call 403f`, `bx=word[bx]` ->
word[0x4b9e], stop on 0 (cursor += 2) or word[0x450]==0 (budget: return without advancing).  403f (asm
0x403f-0x4095): es=word[word[0x156a]] (the viewport's draw segment), di=word[0x6b74] (reticle pixel; -1 =
none): read the pixel, if not 0xff write 0xff, keep the colour in byte[0x6b76] and this node's object
word[bx+2] in word[0x6b72] -- the "object under the reticle" that feeds the target lock; on the live VGA
page (seg == word[0x722]) bracketed by lcall [0x159c]/[0x15a0].  Ghidra typed the pixel offset as a host
char* and compared the segment against &DAT_2000_bfff.  The per-kind rasterizers 29ec/2bb8/2e49/309b/30bc/
30de/3536 (+3425, not in the function set) are the next slices.
